>> Dynamic Routing automatically learns and updates routes between networks using routing protocols. Unlike Static Routing, which requires manual configuration, Dynamic Routing protocols allow routers to communicate and update routes as the network topology changes.

  >> Two classes of Routing protocals
  ✅✅ Distance Vector : Find best path to remote network by judging distance. The route with least hop count is determined as best route. eg : RIP, IGRP

  ✅✅ Link State: also called shortest path first protocal, it maintians 3 tables
       >> 1 table : directly connected neighbors
       >> 2nd table : topology of entire network
       >> 3rd table : routing table

       eg: OSPF, IP
       
  >> Routing Protocal Types:
Dynamic routing protocols are classified into two main categories:

✅✅ 1. Interior Gateway Protocols (IGP)
Used within an Autonomous System (AS) (e.g., inside a company's network).

🔹 Distance Vector Protocols (RIP, EIGRP)
🔹 Link-State Protocols (OSPF, IS-IS)

✅✅2. Exterior Gateway Protocols (EGP)
Used to route traffic between Autonomous Systems (AS) (e.g., between ISPs).

🔹 Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)


