✅✅ VLAN Trunking Protocal(VTP)
🔹 It manages the addition, deletion, and renaming of VLANs.
🔹 VLAN information is shared between switches without manual configuration on each device.
🔹 Prevents mismatched VLAN configurations across switches.
🔹 Reduces Administrative Overhead

📌 📌  VTP Modes
A switch can be configured in one of three VTP modes:

Mode        Function
=======     ===========
Server  - Default mode.
- Can create, delete, and modify VLANs.
- Advertises VLANs to other switches.
- Stores VLAN information in NVRAM.

Client  - Cannot create, delete, or modify VLANs.
- Synchronizes VLAN configuration from VTP servers.
- Stores VLAN information in RAM (not NVRAM).

Transparent - Does not participate in VTP updates.
- Allows manual VLAN configuration.
- Forwards VTP messages without modifying them.

