🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹 2) Dynamic ARP Inspection
>> Dynamic ARP Inspection (DAI) is a security feature that helps protect networks from ARP spoofing attacks by verifying ARP packets. It works in conjunction with DHCP Snooping to ensure only legitimate ARP requests and replies are allowed on the network.

>> Prevents man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks.
Stops IP spoofing by verifying MAC-IP mappings.
Protects network integrity by ensuring only legitimate ARP packets are forwarded.

>> How DAI Works
Validates ARP Packets:

Checks if the MAC-IP pair in an ARP packet matches the DHCP Snooping Binding Table.
Drops ARP packets with invalid or spoofed addresses.


