✅✅ Access Control Lists

🔹 Access Control list is used to apply set of rules to network traffic either to allow or deny the packets based on IP address, protocal and port number. 
🔹 ACLs are commonly used by routers, switches, firewalls to enhace security and traffic control flow.


>> Use Cases of ACLs:
🔹  Traffic Filtering: Restrict access to a network or subnet.
🔹  Security: Block malicious IPs or unauthorized users.
🔹  Quality of Service (QoS): Prioritize specific traffic.
🔹  Network Address Translation (NAT): Define specific rules for translation.

>> ACL types
🔹 Standard
🔹 Extended
🔹 Named

🔹🔹🔹🔹 Standard ACL :
 >> Standard ACL filters traffic only based on "source IP address"
 >> Uses ACL numbers between 1-99 and 1300-1999

 >> Allow specific subnet and deny others
 Router(config)# access-list 10 permit 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255
Router(config)# access-list 10 deny any
Router(config)# interface GigabitEthernet0/0
Router(config-if)# ip access-group 10 in
Router(config-if)# exit

>> Block specific IP address
