     QOS (Quality Of Service)

     >> QoS (Quality of Service) is a set of techniques and mechanisms used in networking to manage and prioritize network traffic, ensuring that critical or latency-sensitive applications (like voice, video, or real-time data) receive the bandwidth and performance they need.

     ✅ Imp workds:
        >> Bandwidth  : Maximum rate of data transfer
        >> Latency : Delay between source and destination
        >> Jitter  : Variation in packet arrival time

     ✅ Why QoS is Important:
        >>In networks, all traffic is treated equally by default. When congestion happens, QoS ensures that high-priority traffic (like VoIP or live video) is not delayed or dropped, while less critical data (like file downloads or emails) may be slowed down or queued.

    🎯 Goals of QoS:
    >> Prioritize traffic (e.g., VoIP > web browsing)
    >> Minimize delay for time-sensitive data
    >> Reduce jitter in streaming/voice communication
    >> Avoid packet loss for critical applications
    >> Control bandwidth usage based on policy


    ✅ QOS Techniques:
    🎯  Classification and Marking :
       >> For a router or switch to give particular level of service to a traffic , it has to recognize the type of traffic first

       >> Common way to recognize traffic are
         >> 1. COS (Class of Service)
                >> Layer 2 service
                >> There is a 3 bit field in 802.1q frame header which is used to carry COS , QOS marking
                >> IP phone signalling calla QOS value = 3
                >> Voice = 5
         >> 2. DSCP(Differenciated Serice Code Point)
                >> Layer 3 service
                >> 6 bits are used in IP header -->4 possible combination
                >> IP phone signalling calla QOS value = 24 (CS3)
                >> Voice = 46(EF)
         >> 3. Access Control List(ACL)
                >> ACS can rexognize traffic based on Layer 2 and Layer3 info
         >> 4. NBAR(Network based application recognition)
                >> NBAR is used to recognise traffic based on layer 3 to layer 7 info


    🎯  Congetion Management:
       >> Queing is used manage congestion on routers and switches
       >> CBWFQ(Class Based Weighted Fair Queing)
       >> LLQ(Low latency queing)

    🎯  Modular QOS CLI:
       >> Class Map  >> which defines the traffic to take an action on
       >> Plocy Map  >> Take the action on the traffic
       >> Serice policy applies the policy to an interface

    🎯 🎯 Configuration

        >> class-map match-any VOICE
           match ip dscp ef

           policy-map PRIORITY-VOICE
           class VOICE
           priority 1000   # Guaranteed bandwidth

           interface GigabitEthernet0/1
           service-policy output PRIORITY-VOICE

